WEBVTT

00:00.562 --> 00:03.982
JULY 12TH (MON) 5:05 PM

00:05.692 --> 00:08.778
Yoshikage… My darling boy…

00:08.903 --> 00:11.780
Where are you?

00:12.157 --> 00:15.952
You must be in hiding, you must've
changed your face, even your name.

00:16.036 --> 00:20.081
My poor son…
I'll make sure they pay dearly…

00:20.832 --> 00:25.086
Right. We need to look further into
the recent missing-person cases.

00:25.420 --> 00:26.963
That's including runaway cases.

00:27.922 --> 00:30.424
Isn't Kira in hiding…

00:30.467 --> 00:34.179
Do you really think he'd continue
on his murdering spree?

00:34.262 --> 00:37.223
Serial killers like him

00:37.265 --> 00:39.642
can't just brush aside
their murderous impulses.

00:39.934 --> 00:41.518
He will kill again.

00:45.273 --> 00:48.651
I wonder if wait and watch
really is the best way to go…

00:48.735 --> 00:52.321
We haven't found a single clue
leading us to Kira.

00:52.364 --> 00:54.407
I've been wondering the same.

00:54.532 --> 00:57.034
But Jotaro did say…

00:57.494 --> 00:59.746
If he finds something,
we spring to action.

00:59.871 --> 01:01.914
Until then, we should go back
to being ordinary students,

01:01.956 --> 01:03.248
according to him.

01:03.291 --> 01:07.336
I'd rather hunt down that bastard
Kira than hit the books.

01:07.420 --> 01:12.049
We almost got him that one time,
it'll be a one-two knockout.

01:10.006 --> 01:13.509
KISARA DRUG

01:13.760 --> 01:16.846
Yes. And since I'm repairing
the fire damage,

01:16.888 --> 01:18.598
I'd like to do some
renovations, too.

01:18.681 --> 01:20.265
That bastard!

01:20.308 --> 01:23.311
He's snapping pictures of people
in search of my son!

01:23.353 --> 01:25.938
I suppose I should
have an estimate.

01:26.147 --> 01:28.107
That numbnut Jotaro
and his fellow Stand users

01:28.149 --> 01:30.067
think they can lay down the law…

01:30.944 --> 01:33.947
I will annhiliate these parasites…

01:33.988 --> 01:36.532
I will give life
to new Stand users…

01:37.951 --> 01:38.785
Hm?

01:38.827 --> 01:39.911
That's…

01:46.501 --> 01:48.419
I know that's him!

01:48.503 --> 01:52.173
Altered appearances cannot
weaken the bond of father and son.

01:52.215 --> 01:54.634
I could never mistake
my son for another!

01:54.676 --> 01:57.345
I've found you, Yoshikage…

02:01.433 --> 02:02.434
<i>I'll find the answer…</i>

02:03.268 --> 02:06.271
<i>I'll identify
this imposter of a dad</i>

02:06.855 --> 02:08.898
It can't be…

02:09.357 --> 02:13.857
At this rate,
those Stand users will…

02:14.028 --> 02:17.239
Never!
It stops now!

02:17.740 --> 02:21.577
With every fiber of my being,
I will protect Yoshikage!

02:23.371 --> 02:25.039
<i>Breakdown, Breakdown</i>

02:25.707 --> 02:27.834
<i>(Listen up)
Breakdown, Breakdown</i>

02:28.585 --> 02:30.545
<i>(Listen)
Breakdown, Breakdown</i>

02:31.796 --> 02:34.882
<i>Breakdown, Breakdown
(3, 2, 1) Let's Go!</i>

02:34.924 --> 02:36.091
JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE
DIAMOND IS UNBREAKABLE

02:36.134 --> 02:40.634
<i>Shining Justice begins to sprout</i>

02:41.681 --> 02:46.181
<i>Brand-new bed town
Will we meet? Let's find out</i>

02:47.353 --> 02:51.853
<i>Feeling the sea breeze from the cape
through the tunnel to the tower</i>

02:52.942 --> 02:57.442
<i>We wander into the alley,
drawn to each other</i>

02:58.239 --> 03:02.739
<i>A shadow melts into our hearts</i>

03:05.622 --> 03:10.122
<i>But the golden spirits
shine a light to protect us</i>

03:15.507 --> 03:20.007
<i>Let the voice of love
take you higher</i>

03:20.512 --> 03:25.012
<i>Let the gathering forces
overcome time itself</i>

03:26.851 --> 03:31.351
<i>1999 Bizarre Summer</i>

03:31.773 --> 03:36.273
<i>Our courage keeps the town in bloom</i>

03:37.362 --> 03:41.532
<i>Great Days</i>

03:43.952 --> 03:46.412
JULY 15TH (THURS) 7:50 AM

03:48.540 --> 03:50.333
See ya later.

03:50.375 --> 03:54.670
EPISODE 31
JULY 15TH (THURS), PART 1

03:50.416 --> 03:53.502
I'm gonna be late…
And I'm class monitor today!

03:55.505 --> 04:00.005
JULY 15TH (THURS), 8:02 AM

04:01.970 --> 04:03.012
I'm exhausted…

04:03.096 --> 04:05.306
I stayed up way too late.

04:05.348 --> 04:09.810
I slept like a rock.
Feeling fit as a fiddle.

04:10.478 --> 04:11.979
Look, Josuke.

04:12.313 --> 04:14.064
Binoculars.

04:14.148 --> 04:16.191
Someone dropped their binoculars.

04:16.234 --> 04:19.195
Well it doesn't take much
to capture your attention.

04:19.404 --> 04:20.947
Gross. Don't pick them up.

04:21.072 --> 04:22.782
What? Gross?

04:22.824 --> 04:25.076
I assure you I am not gross!

04:26.995 --> 04:29.372
Hi, Josuke and Okuyasu.

04:29.497 --> 04:32.666
You again? Don't freak us out
like that, Mikitaka.

04:32.750 --> 04:35.878
My heart can't take
shock like that.

04:35.920 --> 04:37.379
Well, I wouldn't go so far as to…

04:37.505 --> 04:39.381
Easy there. It's not a compliment!

04:39.465 --> 04:42.551
Oh yeah, that's right…
You have perfect timing.

04:42.677 --> 04:46.180
There's something I want you
to come clean on right now.

04:46.222 --> 04:48.891
That whole bit about being
an alien was a lie, right?

04:48.975 --> 04:50.351
You're just a Stand user

04:50.393 --> 04:52.978
who's convinced himself
he's an alien, aren't you?

04:53.021 --> 04:55.231
Quit screwing with us
and be real, dammit!

04:56.065 --> 04:58.192
I have always been real with you.

04:58.234 --> 04:59.735
I am an alien.

04:59.902 --> 05:02.571
Why are you suddenly talking
like some weirdo?

05:02.697 --> 05:03.906
Okay, fine.

05:04.032 --> 05:05.575
Just what are you doing out here

05:05.658 --> 05:08.077
transforming into
a pair of binoculars?

05:08.328 --> 05:09.078
Oh, yes.

05:09.120 --> 05:13.040
I want you two to see something,
hence my waiting here for you.

05:13.374 --> 05:14.416
That?

05:15.835 --> 05:19.296
That… That transmission tower
to be exact.

05:19.380 --> 05:21.256
Transmission tower?

05:21.299 --> 05:23.968
Well, it's not really
a transmission tower anymore.

05:24.052 --> 05:27.472
Without its power lines,
it's more a remnant of the past.

05:27.555 --> 05:29.848
When redevelopment
really took off in Morioh,

05:29.891 --> 05:32.935
most power lines
were moved underground.

05:33.061 --> 05:35.146
What's all this about anyway?

05:35.229 --> 05:38.315
Is that what you're using
to communicate with other planets?

05:38.566 --> 05:42.486
Smoke is wafting up from around
the center of the tower, yes?

05:45.198 --> 05:46.032
Huh?

05:46.074 --> 05:47.950
Y-You're right…

05:49.410 --> 05:51.703
Have a closer look please.

05:59.003 --> 06:01.088
H-Hey, look, it's a kettle!

06:01.130 --> 06:03.590
What? Way up in some tower?!

06:03.633 --> 06:05.760
That's like 20 meters up!

06:05.802 --> 06:06.844
No, a little higher.

06:06.928 --> 06:09.263
Could you please look
about 5 meters above?

06:11.307 --> 06:13.142
What the heck?

06:13.184 --> 06:15.477
L-Let me take a look.

06:24.445 --> 06:27.156
There! Now I see him!

06:27.198 --> 06:28.574
I see a guy!

06:28.616 --> 06:31.577
- He's cooking something!
- What?! Let me see!

06:31.619 --> 06:34.955
That tower… it must be his home.

06:34.997 --> 06:37.541
He looks like he spends
his whole life up there!

06:37.667 --> 06:40.628
He's fishing from the river,
he's even got cucumbers growing.

06:40.795 --> 06:42.546
Clever bastard!

06:42.755 --> 06:47.255
I get it! It's like
a self-sufficient home.

06:48.010 --> 06:51.930
This world has no shortages
of curious individuals, does it.

06:57.729 --> 06:58.730
Look out!

07:05.987 --> 07:07.697
H-He's…

07:07.739 --> 07:09.657
It's a new Stand user!

07:09.824 --> 07:12.201
Yeah! He was definitely flying!

07:12.660 --> 07:16.872
But what's a Stand user
doing living up there?

07:17.039 --> 07:21.539
It appears that man
calls for a closer look.

07:23.713 --> 07:26.632
Well what do we have here…
They've finally arrived.

07:26.799 --> 07:29.551
I wonder whether
I caught their interest?

07:30.011 --> 07:31.262
Don't be shy.

07:31.721 --> 07:35.182
It's been a while since I've
indulged in a little chit chat.

07:35.308 --> 07:39.312
Look. It looks like
he's noticed us, too.

07:39.562 --> 07:41.063
Wanna go look?

07:41.147 --> 07:43.524
Yeah, but play it safe.

07:43.566 --> 07:45.859
We still don't know
whether that Stand user

07:45.902 --> 07:47.820
wants to help or
beat the shit out of us.

07:47.945 --> 07:49.780
JULY 15TH (THURS) 8:05 AM

07:54.869 --> 07:57.913
Huh? Can I help you?

07:57.955 --> 08:01.124
I'm sorry I kinda have to
get going, so…

08:01.209 --> 08:02.919
Huh? Huh?!

08:04.545 --> 08:06.171
JULY 15TH (THURS) 8:11 AM

08:10.092 --> 08:14.592
This thing looks a lot bigger
up close, huh…

08:14.806 --> 08:16.390
You can stop right there, fellas!

08:16.432 --> 08:18.767
I warn you, don't get any closer.

08:18.976 --> 08:19.768
Huh?

08:19.811 --> 08:21.771
I'd move back if I were you.

08:21.813 --> 08:23.773
I just answered the call of nature,

08:23.815 --> 08:26.275
and if you don't stand down,
you won't be happy.

08:27.401 --> 08:28.693
I'm not really following.

08:30.613 --> 08:32.323
D-Don't tell me this is…

08:33.366 --> 08:35.534
Don't say I didn't warn you.

08:35.576 --> 08:37.494
That there is my manure!

08:37.537 --> 08:38.287
Eww, gross!

08:38.412 --> 08:40.497
Gross? That's impolite!

08:40.706 --> 08:43.625
I designed this thing so that
it'd distribute the fertilizer

08:43.709 --> 08:45.836
to all the plants below!

08:46.087 --> 08:49.048
I'm all about zero waste you know.

08:49.298 --> 08:51.466
On the right are
Asiatic day flowers,

08:51.509 --> 08:53.260
mountain asparagus, and watercress.

08:53.302 --> 08:55.721
They're all completely edible!

08:56.013 --> 08:57.889
And with all these plants around,

08:57.932 --> 09:00.643
catching nibbling rabbits
is a cinch,

09:00.726 --> 09:02.561
so I've got the best
of both worlds.

09:02.937 --> 09:05.731
So you really are living up there?

09:06.065 --> 09:09.026
Doesn't this tower belong to
some electric company?

09:09.735 --> 09:11.153
What are you talking about?

09:11.237 --> 09:13.781
I paid for this house
with my own money.

09:14.073 --> 09:17.201
I bought this abandoned tower
for 100,000 yen

09:17.285 --> 09:20.705
and turned it into my dream
self-sufficient house!

09:20.997 --> 09:22.081
Bought?

09:22.123 --> 09:23.415
For 100,000 yen?

09:23.708 --> 09:26.210
That's right, a paltry 100,000 yen.

09:26.294 --> 09:29.672
Since I support myself, I'm not
stuck working for some company.

09:29.714 --> 09:32.174
I don't even have to
leave the house,

09:32.258 --> 09:35.427
and I get all the exercise
I ever need.

09:36.137 --> 09:39.181
Just get a load of
this amazing view.

09:39.265 --> 09:41.350
Huh? W-Wait a minute.

09:41.434 --> 09:42.852
You don't even have to leave?

09:42.894 --> 09:45.187
Just how long have you
been living here?

09:45.438 --> 09:48.023
Let's see…
I suppose about three years now.

09:48.107 --> 09:48.816
Th…

09:48.816 --> 09:49.983
Three years?!

09:50.026 --> 09:53.404
I probably haven't even touched
terra firm a in about a month.

09:53.529 --> 09:55.280
H-Hey, Josuke.

09:55.323 --> 09:56.615
Who knew such a freaking idiot

09:56.657 --> 09:59.701
was here right under
our noses in Morioh.

09:59.827 --> 10:02.162
This guy is just
your ordinary nutcase.

10:02.204 --> 10:03.830
He doesn't wanna hurt us.

10:03.873 --> 10:06.709
No way he's gonna
try and attack us.

10:06.792 --> 10:07.834
You're right…

10:07.877 --> 10:10.296
I guess, for now, heading back
and reporting to Jotaro

10:10.338 --> 10:11.922
is the best option.

10:12.506 --> 10:13.548
Then again…

10:14.342 --> 10:17.345
Something just doesn't feel right…

10:19.013 --> 10:21.765
JULY 15TH (THURS) 10:15 AM

10:27.772 --> 10:30.441
What's he doing?

10:30.524 --> 10:33.568
I suppose children are known
to take videos, too…

10:33.861 --> 10:35.696
But he's clearly hiding
behind that pillar,

10:35.738 --> 10:38.574
like he's up to
the same thing I am.

10:38.866 --> 10:42.911
He's following someone
and capturing their every move…

10:43.287 --> 10:46.415
Could his target be
in this picture?

10:49.627 --> 10:52.254
HAYATO KAWAJIRI

10:50.086 --> 10:52.275
"Hayato Kawajiri," huh…

10:53.214 --> 10:56.300
Something's unusual…

10:56.676 --> 10:58.052
about this kid.

11:04.392 --> 11:06.310
JULY 15TH (THURS) 7:33 AM

11:09.355 --> 11:10.939
I'm home.

11:11.524 --> 11:16.024
SILENCE

11:12.024 --> 11:13.358
Well that's weird.

11:13.651 --> 11:16.967
Josuke, you still haven't
left for school?

11:17.196 --> 11:18.864
Josuke!

11:21.826 --> 11:24.119
God I'm starving.

11:28.332 --> 11:30.500
Josuke, that ungrateful…

11:30.584 --> 11:32.460
He doesn't give a shit
about anybody else!

11:32.545 --> 11:34.713
He takes a giant bite out
of my favorite Kamakura Custar

11:34.755 --> 11:38.216
and plops it back in the fridge
like it never happened?!

11:39.260 --> 11:42.429
There's supposed to be two
in here anyway.

11:42.805 --> 11:45.599
He freak in pisses me off.

11:46.517 --> 11:49.728
JULY 15TH (THURS) 8:14 AM

11:53.315 --> 11:56.985
Hey, something fell out of
your pocket.

11:59.030 --> 12:00.322
Is that a photograph?

12:00.406 --> 12:02.032
Would you mind skedaddling?

12:02.116 --> 12:05.035
Don't worry about picking it up.
I'll get it later.

12:05.327 --> 12:07.620
It looks like a plain old Polaroid.

12:07.663 --> 12:08.830
What's he getting
all worked up for?

12:08.873 --> 12:11.125
It's fine! Just leave!

12:14.253 --> 12:16.213
What?! You're that…

12:16.338 --> 12:18.506
Hey! J-J-Josuke!

12:18.591 --> 12:21.176
You're Kira's old man!

12:21.302 --> 12:24.013
I should've known that bastard
of a ghost dad was behind this!

12:24.638 --> 12:28.516
So you've finally stepped
into my abode. I've been waiting.

12:31.228 --> 12:33.897
Tell someone to come in,
and they get nervous and refuse.

12:33.981 --> 12:36.775
Tell them the opposite,
and they get pissed and enter.

12:36.942 --> 12:40.946
At long last you've entered
into Superfly, Josuke Higashikata!

12:40.988 --> 12:42.072
W-What?!

12:42.281 --> 12:44.700
Well done, Toyohiro Kanedaichi!

12:44.742 --> 12:49.242
You've ensnared that fool Josuke
into Superfly!

12:49.413 --> 12:50.414
Kudos, friend, kudos!

12:50.498 --> 12:54.293
I don't like the looks of this!
Shit… Come back, Josuke!

12:54.335 --> 12:58.422
No, Kira's dad is right there!
He's got the arrow!

13:00.174 --> 13:01.049
You bastard!

13:01.092 --> 13:02.551
You little—

13:03.844 --> 13:05.387
What?!

13:08.182 --> 13:10.726
Once someone steps into
the tower's realm,

13:10.810 --> 13:15.310
it won't spit them out until
its next victim steps in.

13:15.815 --> 13:17.149
If they try to force their way out,

13:17.191 --> 13:20.235
they simply become
a part of the tower.

13:20.444 --> 13:24.698
That's my Stand, Superfly!

13:26.075 --> 13:29.036
We got ya good, Josuke Higashikata!

13:29.078 --> 13:32.414
Keep him in your clutches,
Toyohiro Kanedaichi!

13:35.000 --> 13:37.168
Josuke!

13:41.715 --> 13:44.426
SUPERFLY

13:44.718 --> 13:45.927
Josuke!

13:45.970 --> 13:47.596
Damn it…

13:50.975 --> 13:53.435
Now I did mention it is my Stand,

13:53.602 --> 13:57.689
but Superfly isn't exactly
under my control.

13:57.815 --> 14:00.234
It pretty much does its own thing.

14:00.276 --> 14:02.861
Now that you guys are here,
I can finally take off.

14:03.154 --> 14:07.158
I've been trapped by Superfly
this whole time.

14:07.741 --> 14:11.244
Well, take good care of
the place for me!

14:12.454 --> 14:13.955
Sly sonuvabitch!

14:14.081 --> 14:16.917
So he's in cahoots with
the ghost photograph guy.

14:16.959 --> 14:20.754
Mr. Okuyasu, is there any way
I can be of assistance?

14:20.921 --> 14:23.089
You'll just get hurt,
so stay out of it.

14:23.132 --> 14:25.384
Your job's done.

14:25.467 --> 14:27.969
Now if you could transform into
some dynamite

14:28.053 --> 14:29.804
instead of dice or binoculars,

14:29.847 --> 14:31.974
we might have something
to work with.

14:32.975 --> 14:34.142
That would be impossible.

14:34.226 --> 14:36.811
I can't transform into objects
more powerful than myself,

14:37.062 --> 14:38.480
and explosives,
as well as intricate mechanisms,

14:38.564 --> 14:39.856
are off limits.

14:39.982 --> 14:41.817
But there must be
something I can do.

14:41.901 --> 14:43.110
Shut up.

14:43.235 --> 14:45.987
I already told you there's not
a damn thing you can do.

14:46.071 --> 14:48.406
Leave the aggressive shit to us.

14:49.283 --> 14:52.077
That asshole thinks
he's trapped his prey

14:52.119 --> 14:53.995
while making some amazing escape,

14:54.038 --> 14:56.957
but he clearly doesn't know
who we are.

14:57.458 --> 14:59.960
Hey. You gonna go for it, Okuyasu?

15:00.127 --> 15:02.462
Ready as you are, pal.

15:02.504 --> 15:05.006
This tower's got nothing on us.

15:05.049 --> 15:06.925
Let's bust it up, Josuke!

15:07.927 --> 15:11.847
You know it. Busting out of here
will be a snap!

15:18.854 --> 15:20.438
Whoa there!

15:20.898 --> 15:24.192
The heck?
How'd they get so strong?!

15:24.318 --> 15:26.194
This thing's pretty damn solid.

15:26.278 --> 15:30.778
As long as we keep hitting it,
this thing should snap in two.

15:31.116 --> 15:34.577
And look.
He's about to come crashing down.

15:34.662 --> 15:38.082
Y-You knuckle-heads!
Think you can scare me, huh?

15:38.165 --> 15:40.667
I thought you'd pull
something like that.

15:40.793 --> 15:42.419
Guess you haven't noticed.

15:42.628 --> 15:45.464
This tower has absorbed
your powers,

15:45.506 --> 15:48.717
and redistributed the force
over its entire structure.

15:48.801 --> 15:51.595
Huh? What the hell is
that jackass blathering about?

15:51.679 --> 15:54.890
Josuke, hang tight, I'll have you
out of there in no time!

15:54.974 --> 15:56.100
It's gloves off!

15:56.183 --> 15:58.727
Hold it, Okuyasu. Listen for a sec.

16:04.775 --> 16:09.070
This isn't normal.
What's that weird sound?

16:09.154 --> 16:12.282
That's the sound of the energy
left over from your punches

16:12.366 --> 16:14.951
reverberating throughout the tower.

16:15.160 --> 16:15.910
What?

16:15.995 --> 16:18.080
You may want to consider this…

16:18.122 --> 16:21.083
Ever heard of
the law of conservation?

16:21.125 --> 16:25.625
Energy that is collected
will eventually be released.

16:25.796 --> 16:27.964
I wonder where it's gonna go?

16:28.132 --> 16:29.424
Holy shit…

16:29.717 --> 16:31.593
Get down, Okuyasu!

16:34.888 --> 16:36.097
What?!

16:42.688 --> 16:44.606
Punch the tower
as much as you'd like,

16:44.648 --> 16:47.442
all that energy is just going to go
around and around

16:47.484 --> 16:50.195
and come right back to you.

16:50.321 --> 16:51.613
Strike it, and you'll enjoy
a knuckle sandwich.

16:51.655 --> 16:53.281
Cut it, and you'll need
a few bandaids.

16:53.782 --> 16:55.533
Just think about it.

16:55.576 --> 16:59.580
No matter how powerful or how
amazing one's abilities may be,

16:59.747 --> 17:02.624
this tower cannot be destroyed!

17:04.793 --> 17:05.960
Okuyasu!

17:06.086 --> 17:08.338
I'm starting to worry, Josuke…

17:08.422 --> 17:10.132
I didn't manage to dodge it.

17:10.215 --> 17:12.508
It hollowed out a hole in my side.

17:13.635 --> 17:15.970
Guess I should've warned you, huh…

17:16.013 --> 17:18.348
I bet you guys are thinking that if

17:18.432 --> 17:22.144
you manage to defeat me,
the user, you have a way out.

17:22.436 --> 17:24.104
But that's just another pipe dream.

17:24.271 --> 17:27.232
Remember, this Stand exists
independent of me.

17:27.358 --> 17:29.234
Even if I drop dead,

17:29.276 --> 17:33.280
this tower will likely continue
snaring victims forever.

17:33.447 --> 17:35.657
That's Superfly's specialty.

17:37.451 --> 17:38.410
Josuke…

17:38.452 --> 17:40.495
Forever?

17:42.331 --> 17:44.624
Don't look so serious.

17:44.666 --> 17:48.836
Just find someone else to take
your place, Josuke Higashikata.

17:48.921 --> 17:50.839
One person goes in,
and one person goes out.

17:50.881 --> 17:55.381
Just trap some poor fool
and get yourself out.

17:56.136 --> 17:59.055
It's kinda like
that card game Old Maid.

17:59.348 --> 18:01.224
Actually,
it's a lot like human society.

18:01.433 --> 18:05.186
Just hand over the old maid
to someone else.

18:05.479 --> 18:06.480
Don't you agree?

18:06.522 --> 18:11.022
Pulling someone else in
will certainly help Josuke.

18:11.527 --> 18:12.528
Huh?

18:13.695 --> 18:14.696
What?

18:15.531 --> 18:19.576
Who better to go back than you…
To the tower's realm…

18:19.660 --> 18:21.203
you shall return.

18:22.996 --> 18:23.913
You…

18:23.997 --> 18:26.416
Mikitaka! When did you…

18:26.500 --> 18:28.084
What are you?

18:28.168 --> 18:30.712
How are you a power line?
When did you get there?

18:30.796 --> 18:32.631
What kind of power is this?

18:32.673 --> 18:34.716
Kind of you to ask.

18:35.384 --> 18:38.720
I am in fact an alien.

18:38.804 --> 18:39.721
What?

18:40.013 --> 18:43.391
Now that's what I call
being of assistance!

18:43.475 --> 18:44.559
You must act now.

18:44.643 --> 18:47.062
Please exit the confines
of the tower, Mr. Josuke.

18:47.104 --> 18:48.480
Y-You bastard!

18:48.522 --> 18:50.774
You freak in rock, Mikitaka!

18:50.858 --> 18:52.734
Josuke, get out of there now.

18:52.776 --> 18:54.736
Get out from under the tower!

18:54.778 --> 18:56.237
R-Right…

19:03.287 --> 19:04.246
Hell yeah!

19:04.288 --> 19:06.581
You bastard! What the hell?!

19:06.623 --> 19:09.125
The guy in the photograph
never mentioned

19:09.209 --> 19:11.669
Josuke had any ally like you!

19:12.045 --> 19:16.174
Being an alien, I have no knowledge
of this so-called Old Maid game,

19:16.216 --> 19:20.136
but tricking Josuke and suddenly
telling him he is trapped forever…

19:20.220 --> 19:22.430
appears to me a lot like
an adult beating a child

19:22.473 --> 19:24.766
at a New Year's card game
by cheating.

19:24.850 --> 19:28.270
That is why you should be the
one to remain within the tower.

19:28.896 --> 19:31.023
Here is where you will remain.

19:36.695 --> 19:39.531
You know,
living all this time up here

19:39.573 --> 19:42.117
has given me
these really thick calluses.

19:42.367 --> 19:44.994
They also hold a lot of stuff.

19:45.913 --> 19:46.997
Die dickhead!

19:48.749 --> 19:51.293
You seem to assume that what's
in your hand is a part of me,

19:51.418 --> 19:53.294
but I'm afraid
that's a misconception.

19:53.587 --> 19:55.213
That is not me,

19:55.297 --> 19:59.342
but the power line
you were hanging onto before.

20:03.597 --> 20:04.681
He did it!

20:04.765 --> 20:05.682
All right!

20:05.766 --> 20:08.602
Now get yourself to the top
and get over here, Mikitaka!

20:09.394 --> 20:12.647
After so long, you happened to
step into my tower's realm.

20:12.689 --> 20:14.982
You really think
I'd let you just walk away?

20:15.067 --> 20:17.861
You're looking at a man who's
spent every moment of every day

20:17.945 --> 20:20.447
thinking about escaping this tower!

20:26.787 --> 20:28.330
Did you forget my warning?

20:28.372 --> 20:32.167
This tower will return
any attack back onto the attacker.

20:32.251 --> 20:34.336
That wire is also
a part of this tower!

20:34.545 --> 20:38.549
I severed the line so that
the opening would face you.

20:39.258 --> 20:41.885
Is this the end for me?

20:42.928 --> 20:45.347
M-Mikitaka!
Get your ass out of there now!

20:45.889 --> 20:47.974
I can heal that wound!

20:48.183 --> 20:49.475
Nope, he's staying right here.

20:49.518 --> 20:51.478
I get to leave!

20:53.855 --> 20:55.773
Direction and angle, check.

20:58.944 --> 21:00.779
If you strike it,
it'll strike back.

21:01.947 --> 21:03.365
Mikitaka!

21:03.448 --> 21:04.907
Y-You sick bastard!

21:05.284 --> 21:08.954
You definitely made escaping
a little bit tougher,

21:08.996 --> 21:11.707
but that's all behind me now.

21:11.748 --> 21:15.960
I would guess prying
those suckers out will hurt a bit,

21:16.003 --> 21:18.547
but you'll have all the time
in the world later to heal.

21:18.589 --> 21:21.550
Some of the plants down there
are medicinal, you know.

21:21.675 --> 21:22.801
Evil bastard!

21:22.843 --> 21:24.344
You think you can get away

21:24.386 --> 21:26.388
just cause you stepped
outside the tower?

21:26.430 --> 21:29.391
I'll chase your deceitful ass
to the ends of the earth.

21:29.433 --> 21:31.893
Of course I can get away,
you silly.

21:31.977 --> 21:35.063
You still haven't uncovered
Yoshikage Kira's whereabouts,

21:35.105 --> 21:36.898
am I right?

21:40.819 --> 21:44.113
JULY 15TH (THURS) 10:42 AM

21:50.037 --> 21:52.997
Who is this? I've never seen him
before in my life.

21:52.956 --> 21:56.125
JULY 15TH (THURS) 8:14 AM

21:57.753 --> 21:58.962
JULY 15TH (THURS) 8:14 AM

22:02.799 --> 22:05.092
JULY 15TH (THURS) 10:38 AM

22:20.984 --> 22:23.569
<i>I'll figure out who he is…
I know it.</i>

23:38.854 --> 23:41.898
EPISODE 32
JULY 15TH (THURS), PART 2
